        <p>Lassitude,</p>
        <p>Weakness, Depression, Weariness, Failing Memory, Spots before the Eyes. Impure Blood, Feeble Circulation,</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON EVIDENCE.</p>
        <p>Mr. Thomas Rigby, 121, Church- street, Warrington, says :—" I am grateful for the benefit I have received from Doan's pills, and I have no 9bjection to the facts of my case being published. "For between five and six years I was a great sufferer from kidney complaint, the worst part of the ailment being severe pain in my back, which was often so bad that I could not get about. I was almost afraid to stoop, because it was so difficult to raise myself. "I took medicine for three years, but it did me no good at all. It was different however, when I began with Doan's pills, for they helped me from the first, and gradually brought me back to health. (Signed) Thomas Rigby."</p>
