        <p>G 7 86 392 52 67 CO5 Playcd 29, won 13, lost 11, drawn S.</p>
        <p>NORTHERN LEAGUE COMMITTEE MEETING At a.meeting of the Northern League Committee, held at Huddersfield on Tuesday, Mr. J. Platt (Oldham) presiding, the referee in the Batley v. Runcorn match reported the playing of only forty-seven minutes instead of seventy minutes, as agreed. It was resolved that the match be re-played cn a date mutually agreed upon. Ihe referee in the Leeds v. Bradford match reported the playing of only forty-eight minutes of agreed upon. In the akenee of any application from either club for a replay, the match was ordered to stand. Ebbw Vale were fined 9s. for a late start at Hull against Kingston Rovers on the 9th inst. For a similar offence at Runcorn, on the same d..te, Oldham were fined 3s. and Runcorn 4s. The date of the Warrington v. Hull match was altered from March 13th to February 6th. The following new standing ctder was adopted "No member of the League Committee be allowed to conduct or take part in an inquiry in VI hich the club is interested."</p>
      </div>
