      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-01-23_WidnesExaminer_art0120" n="art0120">
        <head>Street Litter.</head>
        <p>Street Litter.</p>
        <p>Sir,—At a meeting of the Executive Committee com- ments were made by several members upon the preva- lence, particularly during the last few weeks, of waste paper and litter about the streets of the town. No doubt the gusty winds recently experienced have caused much of this, and the season of stocktaking and other sales, when handbills are freely distributed, will also account for a considerable quantity. Still, a great improvement would be effected if the public generally would refrain from thoughtlessly casting away paper in the streets, The Corporation should certainly be supported in their efforts to beautify and to keep in good order the streets in the town.—Yeurs truly, GEORGE H. SMITH, Secretary. Beautiful Warrington Society.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1909-01-23_WidnesExaminer_art0121" n="art0121">
