        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF W ARRIN BRUER OF THII lINIIMPLOYHD. From incoiries I have canoed to be made, I have ascertained tbat great distress prevails in the Town among the families of the Unemployed. I have, through the agency of the Distress Committee, been able to provide temporary relief for some of the most neeessitious ceses, but the Fund at my disposal is now nearly exhausted, and tbe relief which I have been able to render must coon come to an end, unless I can obtain the help of any fellow townsmen. My eft)rts have been directed in the relief of women and children by the distribution of coals, bread, milk and en all quantities of greceries, and great care has been exercised by the officers appointed in relieving only deserving oases. I beg therefore to appeal to my follow townsmen for their help in relieving the deserving poor. Subscriptions msy be cent or paid to the Baraugh Treasurer, flank Ito gee, Sankey Street. WILLIAM JOHN FOII3I-IAW, Mayor.</p>
