        <p>SINIPLE CURE FOR DEAFNESS. A medical book just published describes a German doctor's wonderfully simple cure for deafness and head noises (a real home cure). A limited number of these books have been secured for readers of the Warrington " Examiner," and will be sent free by post by the publisher, M. Franckel, 235, High Holborn, London, W.C. LEFT WITHOUT NOTICE. At the Borough Police Court, on Tuesday, Daniel Rolands, of 20, School-brow, was summoned for having been in arrears of rent and with removing furniture without giving notice.— ;Ir. P. L. Edgar, Winwick-street, owner of the house, said the defendant left without giving any notice what- ever. Ile owed 375. in rent. He thought it was a mean action on the part of the defendant as he had stood by bins in time of trouble.—Defendant stated that he had been out of work for a long time. lie was a slater by troth, and had not done any work for 20 or 30 weeks. He had a wife and two children to keep.—The magistrates decided to adjourn the case for a month, defendant to pay 2s. a week until the debt was cleared off.</p>
